{{!
    @template mod_pagecheck/grade_panel

    The grade and the teacher's comment, as the student reads them on the activity page.

    The grade is shown the way the page count is: the figure large, and how much of the maximum it
    is as a bar beside it. Shown only once there is something to show, so a student waiting to be
    marked sees nothing here rather than an empty box promising a grade.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * hasgrade, value, unit - the grade and what it is out of
    * hasbar, percent - the proportion of the maximum, for a grade out of points
    * gradedon - when it was awarded
    * hasfeedback, feedback - the comment written for the student, already formatted

    Example context (json):
    {
        "hasgrade": true,
        "value": "8,50",
        "unit": "of 10,00",
        "hasbar": true,
        "percent": 85,
        "gradedon": "Graded on 3 September 2026",
        "hasfeedback": true,
        "feedback": "<p>Well argued, but the conclusion needs more of your own reading.</p>"
    }
}}
<div class="pagecheck-panel">
    <div class="pagecheck-panel__head">
        <h3 class="pagecheck-panel__title">{{#str}}gradeheading, mod_pagecheck{{/str}}</h3>
        <span class="pagecheck-panel__meta">{{gradedon}}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="pagecheck-panel__body">
        {{#hasgrade}}
            <div class="pagecheck-hero">
                <div class="pagecheck-count pagecheck-count--grade">
                    <span class="pagecheck-count__value">{{value}}</span>
                    <span class="pagecheck-count__label">{{unit}}</span>
                </div>
                {{#hasbar}}
                    <div class="pagecheck-gauge pagecheck-gauge--grade">
                        <div class="pagecheck-gauge__track">
                            <div class="pagecheck-gauge__fill" style="--pagecheck-fill: {{percent}}%;"></div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                {{/hasbar}}
            </div>
        {{/hasgrade}}
        {{#hasfeedback}}
            <div class="pagecheck-feedback">{{{feedback}}}</div>
        {{/hasfeedback}}
    </div>
</div>
